<title>USA: FHP Int'l Q2 shr rises to $0.42.</title>
<headline>FHP Int'l Q2 shr rises to $0.42.</headline>
<dateline>FOUNTAIN VALLEY, Calif. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended  Six months ended</p>
<p>					 Dec. 31,	     Dec. 31,</p>
<p>		     (In millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				     1996    1995	 1996     1995</p>
<p> Revenues			$1,108  $1,016     $2,207   $2,020</p>
<p>Operating income before</p>
<p>  restructuring charge	 39.5    27.1	 76.5     56.8</p>
<p> Restructuring charge	     0     3.9	    0	9.7</p>
<p>Operating income after</p>
<p>  restructuring charge	 39.5    23.2	 76.5     47.1</p>
<p>Net income attributable to common stock</p>
<p>    Before charge		18.4     9.7	 35.4     20.6</p>
<p>    Including charge	    N/A     7.3	  N/A     14.6</p>
<p>Primary earnings per share</p>
<p>    Before charge		0.44    0.24	 0.84     0.50</p>
<p>    After charge		  N/A    0.18	  N/A     0.36</p>
<p>Fully-diluted earnings per share</p>
<p>    Before charge		0.42    0.28	 0.82     0.58</p>
<p>    After charge		  N/A    0.24	  N/A     0.48</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is FHP International Corp.</p>
<p>On Aug. 4, 1996, the company entered into a definitive agreement to be acquired by PacifiCare Health Systems Inc. The combined company will have nearly four million commercial and Medicare members in 15 states and Guam and total revenue of more than $8.6 billion.  Closing of the transaction is conditioned upon receipt of two remaining regulatory approvals and is expected to take place in mid-February.</p>
